# Canonical route: the combined Fishing + Cooking route, fish first and cook
# what you catch. Cooking starts once Fishing reaches 130: Brilliant
# Smallfish 1-50, Longjaw Mud Snapper 50-100, Bristle Whisker Catfish
# 100-175, Mithril Headed Trout 175-250, Filet of Redgill 250-285, Nightfin
# Soup 285-300. Expert is the Expert Cookbook (Shandrina in Ashenvale,
# Wulan in Desolace); Artisan is the Clamlette Surprise quest in Gadgetzan.
# The companion fishing.guide in this pack fishes the route; this guide
# stands alone too, buying its fish on the Auction House.
#
# Counts follow the page's catches where the page gives them (65 Raw
# Brilliant Smallfish, 90 Raw Longjaw Mud Snapper, 175 Raw Bristle Whisker
# Catfish). Where the page gives no count, the count is estimated from the
# recipe's skill colours in professions.json (orange 1 point a craft,
# yellow about 1 in 2, green about 1 in 4): 60 + 80 Raw Mithril Head Trout,
# about 55 Raw Redgill, about 25 Raw Nightfin Snapper. The page says to buy
# 20 Refreshing Spring Water; this guide buys 25, one per soup.
#
# Spell/item ids resolved from professions.json (built from the Forever
# client tables, build 1.60.1.70532), each cross-checked against the page's
# own material lists:
#   Brilliant Smallfish 7751 (recipe 6325), Slitherskin Mackerel 7752,
#   Longjaw Mud Snapper 7753 (recipe 6328),
#   Bristle Whisker Catfish 7755 (recipe 6330),
#   Mithril Headed Trout 20916 (recipe 17062),
#   Filet of Redgill 18241 (recipe 13941),
#   Nightfin Soup 18243 (recipe 13945).
# Recipe vendors confirmed in the data: Filet of Redgill only from Kelsey
# Yance (Booty Bay), Nightfin Soup only from Gikkix (Steamwheedle Port).
guide forever-professions/cooking
title Cooking 1-300
category Professions
coords era
levels 1-60
zone Azeroth

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Apprentice

section Cooking 1-50

step Learn Cooking
  only Alliance
  zone Stormwind City
  tip Cooking takes no profession slot, so every character can learn it. Stephen Ryback in Stormwind teaches Apprentice Cooking, at any character level. This guide cooks what you catch while fishing: Brilliant Smallfish first, from the fish of your starting lakes. Buy Recipe: Brilliant Smallfish here (Catherine Leland sells it in Stormwind; Tharynn Bouden in Goldshire does too). Cook at any fire: a town hearth or your own Basic Campfire.
  train Cooking Apprentice npc 5482
  buy 6325 x1 nearest

step Learn Cooking
  only Horde
  zone Thunder Bluff
  tip Cooking takes no profession slot, so every character can learn it. Aska Mistrunner in Thunder Bluff teaches Apprentice Cooking, at any character level. This guide cooks what you catch while fishing: Brilliant Smallfish first, from the fish of your starting lakes. Buy Recipe: Brilliant Smallfish here (Sewa Mistrunner sells it in Thunder Bluff; Harn Longcast in Bloodhoof Village does too). Cook at any fire: a town hearth or your own Basic Campfire.
  train Cooking Apprentice npc 3026
  buy 6325 x1 nearest

step Brilliant Smallfish: Auction House
  tip What Brilliant Smallfish takes that the Auction House sells: 65 Raw Brilliant Smallfish, the catch from fishing 1-130. The counts drop by what your bags, bank and mail hold.
  auction 6291 x65

step Brilliant Smallfish: fish
  tip Raw Brilliant Smallfish bites in any starting-area lake or river. Fish it while you level, or take it from your bank.
  collect 6291 x65 anywhere gather Fishing 1

step Brilliant Smallfish (1-50)
  tip Brilliant Smallfish, about 54 cooks to 50. Fished Durotar instead of Mulgore or Elwynn? Cook your Raw Slitherskin Mackerel the same way (Recipe: Slitherskin Mackerel from Zansoa in Sen'jin Village). If you run short of fish, catch and cook a few more.
  learn 7751 "Brilliant Smallfish"
  craft 7751 "Brilliant Smallfish" until 50

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Journeyman

section Cooking 50-100

step Journeyman Cooking
  only Alliance
  zone Stormwind City
  tip Journeyman Cooking raises the cap to 150; it needs skill 50 and no character level. Stephen Ryback in Stormwind teaches it. Buy Recipe: Longjaw Mud Snapper while you are here (Tharynn Bouden in Goldshire sells it too).
  train Cooking Journeyman npc 5482
  buy 6328 x1 nearest

step Journeyman Cooking
  only Horde
  zone Thunder Bluff
  tip Journeyman Cooking raises the cap to 150; it needs skill 50 and no character level. Aska Mistrunner in Thunder Bluff teaches it. Buy Recipe: Longjaw Mud Snapper while you are here (Naal Mistrunner sells it in Thunder Bluff; Lizbeth Cromwell in Undercity does too).
  train Cooking Journeyman npc 3026
  buy 6328 x1 nearest

step Longjaw Mud Snapper: Auction House
  tip What Longjaw Mud Snapper takes that the Auction House sells: 90 Raw Longjaw Mud Snapper, the catch from fishing 1-130. The counts drop by what your bags, bank and mail hold.
  auction 6289 x90

step Longjaw Mud Snapper: fish
  tip Raw Longjaw Mud Snapper bites in starting-area lakes and rivers and in the capital cities. Fish it while you level, or take it from your bank.
  collect 6289 x90 anywhere gather Fishing 1

step Longjaw Mud Snapper (50-100)
  tip Longjaw Mud Snapper, about 60 cooks to 100, and past it: the recipe stays yellow to 110. More Raw Longjaw Mud Snapper comes from the next fishing band if you run short.
  learn 7753 "Longjaw Mud Snapper"
  craft 7753 "Longjaw Mud Snapper" until 100

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Expert

section Cooking 100-175

step Expert Cooking
  only Alliance
  zone Ashenvale
  tip Expert Cooking raises the cap to 225. It is a book, the Expert Cookbook, sold by Shandrina at Mystral Lake in Ashenvale. It needs Cooking 125 and level 20. Read it the moment Cooking hits 125: without it, skill stops at 150 and further cooking gains nothing. Shandrina also sells Nightcrawlers for the fishing that goes with this band.
  level 20
  train Cooking Expert npc 3955

step Expert Cooking
  only Horde
  zone Desolace
  tip Expert Cooking raises the cap to 225. It is a book, the Expert Cookbook, sold by Wulan in Shadowprey Village, Desolace (top floor of the eastern-most building). It needs Cooking 125 and level 20. Read it the moment Cooking hits 125: without it, skill stops at 150 and further cooking gains nothing. Buy 20 Alterac Swiss from Innkeeper Sikewa while you are in Shadowprey Village; the Artisan Cooking quest wants them later.
  level 20
  train Cooking Expert npc 12033

step Bristle Whisker Catfish: recipe
  tip Recipe: Bristle Whisker Catfish, needed for the next band. Naal Mistrunner in Thunder Bluff and Ronald Burch in Undercity sell it for the Horde; Catherine Leland in Stormwind for the Alliance.
  buy 6330 x1 nearest

step Bristle Whisker Catfish: Auction House
  tip What Bristle Whisker Catfish takes that the Auction House sells: 175 Raw Bristle Whisker Catfish, the catch from fishing 75-205. The counts drop by what your bags, bank and mail hold.
  auction 6308 x175

step Bristle Whisker Catfish: fish
  tip Raw Bristle Whisker Catfish bites in the capital cities from Fishing 75 and in the Stonetalon and Ashenvale waters from 130. Fish it while you level, or take it from your bank.
  collect 6308 x175 anywhere gather Fishing 75

step Longjaw Mud Snapper top-up
  tip Still below 100? Cook the Raw Longjaw Mud Snapper from the last fishing band first; Bristle Whisker Catfish needs Cooking 100 to learn. Already at 100, this step is done.
  craft 7753 "Longjaw Mud Snapper" until 100

step Bristle Whisker Catfish (100-175)
  tip Bristle Whisker Catfish, about 140 cooks to 175. Read the Expert Cookbook at 125 if you have not already. More Raw Bristle Whisker Catfish comes from the Dustwallow fishing later if you run short.
  learn 7755 "Bristle Whisker Catfish"
  craft 7755 "Bristle Whisker Catfish" until 175

section Cooking 175-225

step Mithril Head Trout: recipes
  zone Stranglethorn Vale
  tip Kelsey Yance in Booty Bay sells Recipe: Mithril Head Trout and Recipe: Filet of Redgill. Buy both now: the trout recipe cooks next, the Redgill one at 250. Old Man Heming on the lowest dock sells the Expert Fishing book if you are fishing alongside.
  buy 17062 x1 npc 2664
  buy 13941 x1 npc 2664

step Mithril Headed Trout: Auction House
  tip What Mithril Headed Trout takes that the Auction House sells: about 60 Raw Mithril Head Trout for this band, from the Dustwallow Marsh swamp. The counts drop by what your bags, bank and mail hold.
  auction 8365 x60

step Mithril Headed Trout: fish
  tip Raw Mithril Head Trout bites in the Dustwallow Marsh swamp from Fishing 225. Do not fish the ocean there: it gives Raw Rockscale Cod instead. Fish it while you level, or take it from your bank.
  collect 8365 x60 anywhere gather Fishing 225

step Bristle Whisker Catfish top-up
  tip Still below 175? Cook the Raw Bristle Whisker Catfish left from the last band first; Mithril Headed Trout needs Cooking 175 to learn. Already at 175, this step is done.
  craft 7755 "Bristle Whisker Catfish" until 175

step Mithril Headed Trout (175-225)
  tip Mithril Headed Trout, about 60 cooks to 225. Keep the rest of the trout: they cook on after the Artisan Cooking quest.
  learn 20916 "Mithril Headed Trout"
  craft 20916 "Mithril Headed Trout" until 225

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Artisan: Clamlette Surprise

section Cooking 225-300

step Dirge Quikcleave
  only Alliance
  zone Ironforge
  tip Artisan Cooking comes from Dirge Quikcleave in Gadgetzan (Tanaris). The cooking trainer in Ironforge sends you; it needs skill 225 and level 35. Bring the quest goods before you go: 12 Giant Egg, 10 Zesty Clam Meat, 20 Alterac Swiss.
  skill Cooking 225
  level 35
  accept 6612

step Dirge Quikcleave
  only Horde
  zone Orgrimmar
  tip Artisan Cooking comes from Dirge Quikcleave in Gadgetzan (Tanaris). The cooking trainer in Orgrimmar sends you; it needs skill 225 and level 35. Bring the quest goods before you go: 12 Giant Egg, 10 Zesty Clam Meat, 20 Alterac Swiss.
  skill Cooking 225
  level 35
  accept 6611

step Giant Eggs
  zone Tanaris
  tip Giant Eggs drop from the Rocs, Fire Rocs and Searing Rocs of Tanaris. Twelve for the quest.
  collect 12207 x12

step Zesty Clam Meat
  zone Tanaris
  tip Zesty Clam Meat comes from Big-mouth Clams: open each one, every clam holds one. The Steeljaw Snappers on the Tanaris east coast, by Steamwheedle Port, drop the clams. Ten for the quest.
  collect 7974 x10 @66.2,20.8

step Alterac Swiss
  tip Innkeepers and food vendors sell Alterac Swiss; the arrow picks the nearest. Twenty for the quest. The route buys them early (Ben Trias in Stormwind, Innkeeper Sikewa in Shadowprey Village); buy them here if you did not.
  buy 8932 x20 nearest

step Clamlette Surprise
  zone Tanaris
  tip Hand the lead-in to Dirge Quikcleave in Gadgetzan, take Clamlette Surprise, and hand it straight back with the goods: Artisan Cooking is the reward. While you are in Tanaris, ride to Steamwheedle Port and buy Recipe: Nightfin Soup from Gikkix; it finishes the guide at 285.
  turnin 6612 only Alliance
  turnin 6611 only Horde
  accept 6610
  turnin 6610
  buy 13945 x1 npc 8137

step Mithril Headed Trout: Auction House
  tip What the rest of the trout takes that the Auction House sells: about 80 more Raw Mithril Head Trout, from the Dustwallow Marsh swamp. The counts drop by what your bags, bank and mail hold.
  auction 8365 x80

step Mithril Headed Trout: fish
  tip More Raw Mithril Head Trout from the Dustwallow Marsh swamp, or take it from your bank.
  collect 8365 x80 anywhere gather Fishing 225

step Mithril Headed Trout (225-250)
  tip Mithril Headed Trout, about 80 more cooks to 250. The recipe goes green at 235, so the last points come slowly.
  craft 20916 "Mithril Headed Trout" until 250

step Filet of Redgill: Auction House
  tip What Filet of Redgill takes that the Auction House sells: about 55 Raw Redgill. The counts drop by what your bags, bank and mail hold.
  auction 13758 x55

step Filet of Redgill: fish
  tip Raw Redgill bites on the coasts fished while hunting the four Nat Pagle quest fish (Stranglethorn Vale, Desolace, Swamp of Sorrows): keep the bycatch, or take it from your bank.
  collect 13758 x55 anywhere gather Fishing 225

step Filet of Redgill (250-285)
  tip Filet of Redgill, about 55 cooks to 285. The recipe came from Kelsey Yance in Booty Bay; if you did not buy it there, no other vendor sells it.
  learn 18241 "Filet of Redgill"
  craft 18241 "Filet of Redgill" until 285

step Nightfin Soup: shopping
  tip Nightfin Soup takes one Refreshing Spring Water a soup. Buy 25 from any innkeeper.
  buy 159 x25 nearest

step Nightfin Soup: Auction House
  tip What Nightfin Soup takes that the Auction House sells: about 25 Raw Nightfin Snapper, caught fishing Feralas at night. The counts drop by what your bags, bank and mail hold.
  auction 13759 x25

step Nightfin Soup: fish
  tip Raw Nightfin Snapper bites in Feralas, but not between 12:00 and 18:00 game time: fish mornings, evenings or nights, or take it from your bank.
  collect 13759 x25 anywhere gather Fishing 255

step Nightfin Soup (285-300)
  tip Nightfin Soup, about 25 cooks to 300. Short of snapper? Cook the rest of the Raw Redgill into Filet of Redgill too, or fish more outside the afternoon, or buy Raw Nightfin Snapper on the Auction House.
  learn 18243 "Nightfin Soup"
  craft 18243 "Nightfin Soup" until 300
